  "summary": "Inspect and function-test the rear-window brake-light circuit for overheating and inoperability; the melted lamp indicates a possible electrical/thermal fault and safety concern.",
  "rationale": "No rulebook entry or similar case matches. The narrative reports a 2025 Ford Maverick whose rear-window brake light was inoperable and had melted while the vehicle was parked, pointing to an electrical or thermal fault in that brake-light circuit. A recall exists for trailer-module brake/turn-signal loss on 2025 Maverick, but it does not describe a melted rear-window brake lamp, so a standard circuit inspection and functional test is appropriate. Because the brake light failed and melted, this is safety-relevant and should be reviewed by a human before any test is booked.",
